Procedure / Steps
1. Open Remix IDE at https://remix.ethereum.org.

2. Open File Explorer and create a new Solidity file named StudentData.sol.

3. Write the Solidity program using the following constructs:
- Structure: To store student details such as roll number, name, age and course.
- Array: To store multiple student records.
- Fallback: To execute when an unknown function is called or ETH is sent with unmatched data.
4. Open the Solidity Compiler tab.

5. Select Solidity compiler version 0.8.20 or a compatible version and click Compile StudentData.sol.

6. After successful compilation, open the Deploy & Run Transactions tab.

7. Select Remix VM (Prague) as the execution environment.

8. Select StudentData from the contract dropdown and click Deploy.

9. After successful deployment, expand the contract under Deployed Contracts.

10. Use the addStudent() function to add student details.

    Example:
Parameter	Value
Roll No	101
Name	Rahul
Age	25
Course	BCT

11. Click Transact to store the student record on the blockchain.

12. Repeat the addStudent() operation to add another student.

13. Use getStudentCount() to display the total number of students stored in the array.

14. Use getStudent(index) or students(index) to retrieve student details using the array index.

15. Test the fallback function by sending a transaction with unmatched function data. Set the Value to 0 Wei and use the low-level transaction interface to call the contract with unmatched data.

16. Observe the transaction details in the Transaction Recorder.

17. Click the transaction details to observe:
- Gas Limit
- Gas Used
- Gas Price
- Transaction Fee
18. Record the observed gas values and transaction fees in the practical journal.
